      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1962375
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-19T23:20:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Why `topdown\u003dFalse`?\n\nFor some reason I thought the output of `os.stat()` of a directory would not correctly reflect that of the subdirectories if the walk is done top-down, but this does not seem to be the case. Modified back to the default `topdown\u003dTrue`.\n\n\u003e so I think we need to intoduce some sorting to make this deterministic\n\nWouldn\u0027t sorting `output` in L54 (return statement) make this deterministic?\n\n\u003e Also we need `followlinks\u003dFalse`\n\nGood point, I believe `followlinks` is `False` by default though.",
      "parentUuid": "19082574_28d19171",
      "revId": "4b046959b69004f24220965b910a09c4fdf38725",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
